1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,954
In this lesson, we'll meet differential
equations, equations that involve a

2
00:00:04,954 --> 00:00:06,869
function and its derivatives.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,779
A differential equation relates an unknown
function to its rate of change.

4
00:00:13,229 --> 00:00:19,095
d y d x equals three y says the rate is
always three times the current value.

5
00:00:20,233 --> 00:00:25,972
To check a solution, substitute it in. Is
y equals e to the three x a solution?

6
00:00:26,422 --> 00:00:31,073
y prime is three e to the three x, which
equals three y. Yes.

7
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:37,512
The general solution includes a constant:
y equals C e to the three x.

8
00:00:37,962 --> 00:00:41,973
Each value of C gives a different curve, a
family of solutions.

9
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:48,924
An initial condition picks one. If y of
zero equals five, then C equals five.

10
00:00:49,374 --> 00:00:52,937
That's a particular solution to the
initial value problem.

11
00:00:54,067 --> 00:01:00,873
Differential equations model the world. A
population growing in proportion to its

12
00:01:00,873 --> 00:01:03,731
size satisfies d P d t equals k P.

13
00:01:04,181 --> 00:01:10,474
Newton's law of cooling says d T d t
equals negative k times T minus the room

14
00:01:10,474 --> 00:01:11,455
temperature.

15
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,147
Your turn. Is y equals x squared a
solution of x y prime equals two y?

16
00:01:18,597 --> 00:01:20,133
Pause the video and try it.

17
00:01:20,583 --> 00:01:25,809
x times two x is two x squared, and two y
is two x squared. Yes.

18
00:01:26,933 --> 00:01:31,370
In this lesson, we'll visualize
differential equations with slope fields.

19
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:35,870
A differential equation tells you the
slope at every point.

20
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:40,971
Draw a short segment with that slope at
many points, and you have a slope field.

21
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:49,441
For d y d x equals x plus y: at zero, zero
the slope is zero. At one, zero it's one.

22
00:01:49,441 --> 00:01:52,937
At zero, negative one it's negative one.

23
00:01:53,387 --> 00:01:54,774
Repeat across a grid.

24
00:01:55,900 --> 00:02:00,316
A solution curve follows the segments,
like a leaf floating on a current.

25
00:02:00,766 --> 00:02:04,158
Start at the initial condition and flow
along the field.

26
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:11,250
To match a field to an equation, check
easy places. If slopes depend only on x,

27
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:13,961
each column of segments is parallel.

28
00:02:14,411 --> 00:02:17,931
If slopes depend only on y, each row is
parallel.

29
00:02:19,066 --> 00:02:24,022
Where the slope is always zero along a
horizontal line, that line is an

30
00:02:24,022 --> 00:02:25,488
equilibrium solution.

31
00:02:25,938 --> 00:02:33,032
For d y d x equals y times two minus y, y
equals zero and y equals two are

32
00:02:33,032 --> 00:02:34,087
equilibria.

33
00:02:35,233 --> 00:02:40,822
Your turn. For d y d x equals x minus y,
what's the slope at two, three?

34
00:02:41,272 --> 00:02:42,808
Pause the video and try it.

35
00:02:43,258 --> 00:02:45,136
Two minus three, negative one.

36
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:51,243
In this lesson, we'll solve differential
equations exactly by separating the

37
00:02:51,243 --> 00:02:51,898
variables.

38
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:59,440
If d y d x equals a function of x times a
function of y, move all the y's to one

39
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:02,163
side and all the x's to the other.

40
00:03:02,613 --> 00:03:04,213
Then integrate both sides.

41
00:03:05,333 --> 00:03:11,733
Solve d y d x equals x over y. Separate: y
d y equals x d x.

42
00:03:12,183 --> 00:03:17,977
Integrate: y squared over two equals x
squared over two plus C. So y squared

43
00:03:17,977 --> 00:03:21,484
minus x squared equals a constant:
hyperbolas.

44
00:03:22,633 --> 00:03:27,433
With y of zero equals three: nine minus
zero equals the constant.

45
00:03:27,883 --> 00:03:33,707
y squared equals x squared plus nine, and
since y starts positive, y equals the

46
00:03:33,707 --> 00:03:36,288
square root of x squared plus nine.

47
00:03:37,433 --> 00:03:44,366
Solve d y d x equals two x y. Separate: d
y over y equals two x d x.

48
00:03:44,816 --> 00:03:50,789
ln absolute y equals x squared plus C, so
y equals A e to the x squared.

49
00:03:51,933 --> 00:03:59,037
Dividing by y assumes y isn't zero. Check:
y equals zero also solves the equation.

50
00:03:59,487 --> 00:04:01,727
Here it's included when A equals zero.

51
00:04:02,866 --> 00:04:08,711
Your turn. Solve d y d x equals y squared
with y of zero equals one.

52
00:04:09,161 --> 00:04:10,697
Pause the video and try it.

53
00:04:11,147 --> 00:04:18,339
Negative one over y equals x plus C, with
C equal to negative one. So y equals one

54
00:04:18,339 --> 00:04:19,830
over one minus x.

55
00:04:20,966 --> 00:04:25,830
In this lesson, we'll solve the most
important differential equation of all:

56
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,622
rate proportional to amount.

57
00:04:28,766 --> 00:04:35,635
d y d t equals k y. If k is positive, the
quantity grows; if negative, it decays.

58
00:04:36,085 --> 00:04:40,544
Bacteria, compound interest and
radioactive atoms all follow it.

59
00:04:41,666 --> 00:04:48,180
Separate and integrate: the solution is y
equals y zero e to the k t, where y zero

60
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:50,007
is the starting amount.

61
00:04:50,457 --> 00:04:52,569
Every solution is an exponential.

62
00:04:53,699 --> 00:04:57,539
A culture grows from one hundred to three
hundred in two hours.

63
00:04:57,989 --> 00:05:04,080
Three hundred equals one hundred e to the
two k, so k equals ln three over two,

64
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,776
about point five five.

65
00:05:06,899 --> 00:05:13,145
Half-life is the time to fall to half: t
equals ln two over the absolute value of

66
00:05:13,145 --> 00:05:13,299
k.

67
00:05:13,749 --> 00:05:19,876
Carbon fourteen has a half-life of five
thousand seven hundred thirty years, so k

68
00:05:19,876 --> 00:05:23,733
is about negative point zero zero zero one
two one.

69
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:31,912
Newton's law of cooling, d T d t equals
negative k times T minus T room, gives T

70
00:05:31,912 --> 00:05:37,901
equals T room plus T zero minus T room,
times e to the negative k t.

71
00:05:38,351 --> 00:05:41,721
The difference from room temperature
decays exponentially.

72
00:05:42,866 --> 00:05:48,887
Your turn. A substance decays with k
equals negative point zero five per year.

73
00:05:48,887 --> 00:05:50,354
Find its half-life.

74
00:05:50,804 --> 00:05:52,340
Pause the video and try it.

75
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:57,334
ln two over point zero five, about
thirteen point nine years.

76
00:05:58,466 --> 00:06:03,876
In this lesson, a BC topic, we'll
approximate a solution numerically, step

77
00:06:03,876 --> 00:06:04,461
by step.

78
00:06:05,599 --> 00:06:10,520
Start at the initial point. Follow the
tangent line for a short step, then

79
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:12,981
recompute the slope there and repeat.

80
00:06:13,431 --> 00:06:17,164
It's like walking a path by checking the
compass every few steps.

81
00:06:18,299 --> 00:06:25,696
With step size h: the next x is x plus h,
and the next y is y plus h times the slope

82
00:06:25,696 --> 00:06:26,577
f of x, y.

83
00:06:27,027 --> 00:06:30,952
y new equals y old plus h times d y d x.

84
00:06:32,099 --> 00:06:39,550
Approximate y of one for d y d x equals x
plus y, y of zero equals one, using h

85
00:06:39,550 --> 00:06:41,059
equals one half.

86
00:06:41,509 --> 00:06:47,980
First step: slope one, so y at one half is
one point five. Second step: slope two, so

87
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:52,624
y at one is one point five plus one, which
is two point five.

88
00:06:53,766 --> 00:06:59,681
The true value is two e minus two, about
three point four four. Smaller steps give

89
00:06:59,681 --> 00:07:00,763
better answers.

90
00:07:01,213 --> 00:07:05,523
With h equals point one, Euler gives about
three point one nine.

91
00:07:06,666 --> 00:07:11,592
If the solution is concave up, the tangent
lines lie below it, and Euler

92
00:07:11,592 --> 00:07:12,618
underestimates.

93
00:07:13,068 --> 00:07:17,377
Here, y double prime is positive, so our
estimates are too low.

94
00:07:18,499 --> 00:07:24,391
Your turn. Take one Euler step of size
point two for d y d x equals two x,

95
00:07:24,391 --> 00:07:26,222
